{#
    NOVA Product Options — src/views/partials/product/options.twig
    Confirmed (docs.salla.dev/422561m0): `product.options` is loopable,
    and this section sits between the confirmed hooks
    `product:single.form.start` / `product:single.form.end`. Rather than
    hand-build every option type (text, dropdown, image swatch, etc.) from
    an unconfirmed field shape, this delegates to the official
    <salla-product-options> web component (confirmed name,
    docs.salla.dev/422688m0), which is Salla's own ready-made component
    for exactly this.

    Note: the fetched doc's own description of what falls between
    form.start/form.end was somewhat ambiguous (it describes the enclosed
    part as "options, and the product price and quantity" but separately
    mentions a second section for "price and availability" too) — kept
    options+price+quantity+CTA together inside the hooks as the more
    defensible reading; verify against a live theme if precision matters.
#}

{% hook 'product:single.form.start' %}

<salla-product-options
    product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    class="nova-product-options"
></salla-product-options>

<div class="nova-product-single__price">
    {% include 'partials/product/price.twig' %}
</div>

<div class="nova-product-single__cart-row">
    <salla-quantity-input class="nova-quantity-input"></salla-quantity-input>

    <salla-add-product-button
        product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        product-status="{{ product.status | default('sale') }}"
        product-type="{{ product.type | default('product') }}"
        class="nova-product-single__cta"
    ></salla-add-product-button>
</div>

{% hook 'product:single.form.end' %}
